# Parity loop (two oracles)

Canonical runbook: [kparser2/docs/report-oracle.md](kparser2/docs/report-oracle.md). Do not write the user a cast/chat script. Echo via `kparser2.cli echo` only when one sample is blocking.

**Wire question:** did this packet mean what we classified? Horizon NDJSON, XiPackets, VieweD, `msg.lua`. `--assert-settled` lives here. Never edit kparser ParseCodes.

**Product question:** should this tab match kparser analytics (#4)? If both sides saw the same melee/kill/XP and numbers disagree, kparser tab meaning wins. Implement in kparser2. Score live `DetailedReports.format`, not unused report skeletons.

## Dual capture is a gate

A report-oracle scan records **both**:

1. Last-green `develop` `kparser2.cli record` (not session WIP) under `ffxi-captures/ndjson/`.
2. `kparser.cli capture` (RAM ChatLines at `0x0062D8F0`) to a sibling chatlines file.

Do **not** mark v1 “unobserved” and proceed. Failed attach: build/elevate/retry; ask once for Administrator. Town idle with a live attach is OK. NDJSON combat/chat with a dead chatlines file is capture broken — fix it; do not classify as kparser-only.

`kparser.cli snapshot` of a file is not attach. Dual-dump of constructed Motenten fixtures is not Horizon layout. RC / `--assert-settled` still does not require v1.

## Ticks (no sleeper)

The long-lived jobs are `record` and `capture`. Attach `notify_on_output` to `record checkpoint:` / `recording stopped:` (and capture checkpoint/stop). Do **not** arm `Start-Sleep` + `AGENT_LOOP_WAKE`. Cursor `/loop` in this repo means record/watch stdout, not a sleeper.

On `record checkpoint:`, run `kparser2/scripts/opcode-heat.ps1` first. Exit 0 (`HEAT unchanged`) means skip reconcile and snapshot. Town position/entity spam and extra yells of an already-seen Kind are not a parity change. Do not infer chocobo digging from a town zone name; the server list is `diggingZoneList` in `server/scripts/globals/hobbies/chocobo_digging/logic.lua`.

Heat change, first checkpoint, or stop: `reconcile-capture.ps1`, snapshot **both** sides, classify **before coding**: kparser2-missing ingest | kparser2-missing report | kparser-only (do not clone) | kparser2-extra (keep) | intentional fork (write down; default match kparser report meaning). Search open PRs. One family on `cursor/session-yyyymmdd-hhmm` from `develop`; draft PR into `develop`, never `main`.

A game DC, kpacket unload, or incoming `0x000B` with `LogoutState` LOGOUT/TIMEOUT/GMLOGOUT **ends that pair**. Zone change is the same opcode (`LogoutState=2`) — keep both files. Then `wait-kpacket-session.ps1` and start a **new** NDJSON plus a **new** chatlines capture. Stop if the user ends the run.

## Wire lookup

Ground truth for classification is Horizon bytes. On mismatch look up XiPackets `0x0017` / `0x0028`, VieweD, `server/scripts/enum/msg.lua`, `spell_list.sql`. Do not give the user an in-game checklist. Do not reopen kparser2 #10–#13. Do not close #4/#6/#9 from a scan. Do not touch #6.
